[block
  'ORD-0006-rules-cache'
  [ctx
    'the spec of EMS-002'
    '.guidelines/.orders/EMS-002/EMS-002.pgml'
  [/ctx]
  [tgt
    'the compiled rules leave the rules store, question 3 of the EMS-001 return, answered a'
  [/tgt]
  [ctx
    'rules.js and burn.js hang the compiled rules on the store object as __compiled, enumerable, so the envelope stores.rules is the digest of the store and the engine cache together, and the Rust reproduces it with glyph_rules::with_cache'
  [/ctx]
  [cnst
    'the JS first: the compiled rules are kept beside the store, keyed by it, and the store object is never written'
  [/cnst]
  [cnst
    'the snapshot moves by decision, the answer a of question 3, and the decision is written; an xml or hgml hash that moves is a regression, not the decision'
  [/cnst]
  [cmp
    'the JS first'
    'the JS keeps its compiled rules off the store object, and the envelope hashes the rules store alone'
    [ctx[/ctx]
    [cnst[/cnst]
  [/cmp]
